On 7 May 2010 08:13, tijlan <jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:

> On 6 May 2010 20:34, Luke Bergen <lukeabergen@gmail.com> wrote:
>
>> hmmm.  So tijlan, you say that you see {lo plise} as being an implicit
>> abstraction of the form {lo nu da plise}.  But then you say that it doesn't
>> make sense to say {mi nelci lo plise} because {lo plise} is not an
>> abstraction.  Pick a lane already  =p
>>
>
> I'm not saying that {mi nelci lo plise} doesn't make sense. I'm saying:
>
>  1) the assumption that "an object and an event are different" does not
> reflect what "an object" actually is
>
> and therefore
>
>  2) the assumption that some particular sumti should be *either* "an
> object" or "a state" does not make sense.
>

"state" and "event" are interchangeabale in this case.

